caption: Keyboard shortcuts
title: Keyboard shortcuts
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Summary
Bind keyboard shortcuts to modal actions using the core `$:/tags/KeyboardShortcut` tag.

! Detail
HyperGSD ships four shortcut triggers, each a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/KeyboardShortcut` with a `key` field naming a shortcut definition in `$:/config/ShortcutInfo/`:

| !Trigger | !Shortcut tiddler | !Action |
|`ui/shortcuts/new-action-trigger` |`((hgsd-new-action))` |Open the new-item modal for an action (clears inherited project, focuses the title field) |
|`ui/shortcuts/new-project-trigger` |`((hgsd-new-project))` |Open the modal for a project (focuses the title field) |
|modal submit |`((hgsd-modal-submit))` |Create from the modal |
|modal close |`((hgsd-modal-close))` |Cancel the modal |

Add your own by copying the pattern: tag the trigger with `$:/tags/KeyboardShortcut`, set `key: ((my-shortcut))`, and create the `$:/config/ShortcutInfo/my-shortcut` tiddler users edit to choose the actual key.

! Best Practice
Shortcuts that open the modal should clear the fields they do not want inherited (see the shipped triggers' `<$action-deletefield>` calls).